# LLVM-COORD — Assignment, isolation, INT results

File: openOODA/audit/plan_llvm_coord.oot
COORD rollup template. This file does not implement emit.
C emit + gcc remains the product path. Do not overwrite oodac/oodac.
Pin: v0.205.0-beta. Lane: LLVM emit only.
Contract: audit/plan_llvm_phalanx.oot

Logline: Twelve roles each own one job and disjoint write paths. INT fills the results table after the smokes run.
Setup: Product compiler is ooda/oodac/oodac. Side ELF is .ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/oodac_llvm. Shared main.oo and cli_emit.oo stay unedited.
Beats:
  1. Restate the observe fact from the phalanx contract.
  2. Assign one job and disjoint files to each of the twelve roles.
  3. Leave the INT results table blank.
  4. Name the run order, the refuse set, and residual facts.

## 1. Observe

  Cold `check fixtures/hello.oo` on an LLVM-linked oodac printed
  `ERR	check	empty` because `llvm_emit_expr` lowered `match`
  expressions to `%OoStr zeroinitializer`.
  `load_expand` does `let src = match read_file { Ok(s) => s, ... }`.
  Empty src hits `check_drive` and prints that line.
  Stamp-walk of a valid listing still worked (no match expr).

## 2. Roles (one job, disjoint files)

| Role | Job | Owns |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| DE1 | Lower match expr to extractvalue and phi | oodac/llvm_emit_match_expr.oo, oodac/llvm_emit_expr.oo |
| DE2 | Close call and method leftovers | oodac/llvm_emit_method.oo, oodac/llvm_fntab.oo |
| RT | Compare C ABI to LLVM preamble | audit/plan_llvm_rt.oot |
| PV1 | Hostile-mutate hello; refuse stale OK | scripts/open68_pv1_hostile.oo |
| PV2 | Prove a planted g_ listing is not required | scripts/open68_pv2_plant.oo |
| SEC | Audit shim and capability grants | audit/plan_llvm_sec.oot |
| MEM | Audit ARC on match and check | audit/plan_llvm_mem.oot |
| INT | Run smokes and the C path | .ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/int_llvm/ |
| HARN | Own phase 1–3 and match-expr smokes | scripts/open68_cold_hello_smoke.oo, scripts/open68_main_check_smoke.oo, scripts/open68_cmds_floor_smoke.oo, scripts/open68_match_expr_smoke.oo |
| HYG | Line lock <=256; report unless over | audit/plan_llvm_hyg.oot |
| DOCS | Boards after INT proof | audit/plan_llvm_docs.oot |
| COORD | Assign, rebuild side ELF, rollup | audit/plan_llvm_coord.oot, audit/plan_llvm_phalanx.oot, .ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/coord_llvm_rebuild.log |

  RT extra, only if the ABI note proves a mismatch: `oodac/llvm_emit_preamble.oo`
  or LLVM decls in `runtime/chs_rt.h`. Not both roles. Not `c_emit*.oo`.
  HYG extra, only if a write-set file exceeds 256 and COORD names that file.
  DOCS extra, only after every INT verdict is PASS: leftover rows in
  `SHIPPED.oot` and `ROADMAP.oot`. Do not write those boards in this turn.
  INT fills only the blank cells in section 6 of this file (COORD-serialized).

## 3. Collision check

  Method: extract every write path from section 2.
  Compare role to role. A shared path is a collision.

  Result: no two roles share a write path. Status: done.

  Slice notes (still one owner each):
    COORD rebuild log is not the INT log directory.
    SEC reads `oodac/llvm_link_shim.oo`. SEC does not edit it.
    MEM reads match and check emit. MEM does not edit DE1 or DE2 files.
    HARN does not own the PV scripts.
    `oodac/main.oo` and `oodac/cli_emit.oo` have no owner this cycle.

## 4. Forbidden

  No `.py` `.sh` `.md` `.js`.
  No `c_emit*.oo`. No `wasm_emit*.oo`. No `x86_emit.oo`.
  No lex, parse, check, or tc writes.
  Do not copy `bin/ooda` onto `oodac/oodac`.
  Do not overwrite `oodac/oodac` with the side ELF.
  Do not retire C emit + gcc.
  Do not plant `.ooda-cache/check/g_*` to make a check print `OK`.
  Do not edit `SHIPPED.oot` or `ROADMAP.oot` before INT proof.

## 5. Order

  Do not race two side-ELF rebuilds.

  1. DE1 match emit. `emit-llvm` of `fixtures/open68_match_expr.oo`
     must write `extractvalue` and `phi`, not a `KW_MATCH` zeroinitializer stub.
  2. DE2 method and fntab leftovers. No variadic `(...)` declare.
  3. RT ABI note. Runtime or preamble write only if ABI is wrong.
  4. COORD rebuild `.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/oodac_llvm`.
     Log: `.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/coord_llvm_rebuild.log`.
  5. HARN keep the four named smokes honest.
  6. PV1 hostile mutate. PV2 planted-`g_` refuse.
  7. SEC shim note. MEM ARC note.
  8. INT run section 6 commands from `ooda/` and fill the table.
     Double-run the four HARN smokes.
  9. HYG line lock on the write set.
  10. DOCS boards only if section 6 is all PASS.

## 6. Results (INT fills)

  Drive the HARN and PV scripts with product `./oodac/oodac run`.
  The check target is the side ELF, not `oodac/oodac`.
  Hang budget: 60s hello, 240s main. Verdict is PASS, FAIL, or MISSING.
  Leave exit, mark, and verdict blank until the live run.

| # | proof | command | exit | mark | verdict |
| ---: | :--- | :--- | ---: | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | side ELF exists | `test -x .ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/oodac_llvm` |  |  |  |
| 2 | phase 1 cold hello | `scripts/open68_cold_hello_smoke.oo` |  |  |  |
| 3 | phase 2 check main | `scripts/open68_main_check_smoke.oo` |  |  |  |
| 4 | phase 3 cmds floor | `scripts/open68_cmds_floor_smoke.oo` |  |  |  |
| 5 | emit lock match | `scripts/open68_match_expr_smoke.oo` |  |  |  |
| 6 | C path check hello | `./oodac/oodac check fixtures/hello.oo` |  |  |  |
| 7 | C path emit-c hello | `./oodac/oodac emit-c fixtures/hello.oo` |  |  |  |
| 8 | PV1 hostile mutate | `scripts/open68_pv1_hostile.oo` |  |  |  |
| 9 | PV2 planted g_ | `scripts/open68_pv2_plant.oo` |  |  |  |
| 10 | double-run phase 1 | `scripts/open68_cold_hello_smoke.oo` |  |  |  |
| 11 | double-run phase 2 | `scripts/open68_main_check_smoke.oo` |  |  |  |
| 12 | double-run phase 3 | `scripts/open68_cmds_floor_smoke.oo` |  |  |  |
| 13 | double-run match | `scripts/open68_match_expr_smoke.oo` |  |  |  |

  Logs: `.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/int_llvm/`. Do not write product files.

## 7. Residual

  These facts stay residual. They are not this lane.

  - LLVM-linked oodac as the gcc replacement. C path stays product.
  - Clang link of full oodac. Lock: `scripts/open68_llvm_lock.oo`.
  - Call or block match expressions. IDENT or STRING arms only.
  - Warm stamp-walk of a valid listing is already product.

## 8. Isolation

  Topology: 12-role phalanx (fan-out).
  Files: disjoint. WORKFLOW section 2 holds by path, not by tree.
  Solo: no. The contract named twelve roles.
  COORD wrote only this file this turn.
  COORD did not edit `SHIPPED.oot`, `ROADMAP.oot`, or product code.
  COORD does not implement emit.

## 9. Next

  Wait for DE1 and DE2 writes. Then rebuild the side ELF.
  INT does not fill section 6 until that ELF exists.
  Do not claim hello-check PASS with a planted `g_` listing.
  Do not copy `bin/ooda` onto `oodac/oodac`.
